From: Pixelado Dev <350114043+pixeladodev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LAN: the ACK sent again goes in one datagram with the CMD

As a host, each CMD is preceded by the previous exchange's ACK sent again (0010, so a client that missed it isn't
left waiting). It went out as its own datagram: one sendto and one radio frame more per exchange (Mario Party DS:
~230 a second). Now it is queued in ENet without a flush, and the CMD's flush sends both in one datagram; the
client gets them in the same order as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/net/LAN.cpp b/src/net/LAN.cpp
index 6fbc4fb..0a8a460 100644
--- a/src/net/LAN.cpp
+++ b/src/net/LAN.cpp
@@ -1716,7 +1716,7 @@ void LAN::SendNow(u32 type, const u8* packet, int len, u64 timestamp)
         enet_peer_send(LastHostPeer, Chan_MP, enetpacket);
     else
         enet_host_broadcast(Host, Chan_MP, enetpacket);
-    enet_host_flush(Host);
+    if (!HoldFlush) enet_host_flush(Host);
 }
 
 int LAN::RecvPacketGeneric(u8* packet, bool block, u64* timestamp)
@@ -1912,7 +1912,11 @@ void LAN::ResendAck(u64 cmdts)
 {
     // only the ACK of the exchange just before this CMD (emulated time restarts with each game)
     if (!LastAckValid || LastAck.empty() || LastAckTS >= cmdts || cmdts - LastAckTS > 100000) return;
+    // Pixelado 0012: not sent on its own: queued in ENet and sent with the CMD that follows, in one datagram (one
+    // sendto and one radio frame less per exchange; the client gets both, in this order, as before)
+    HoldFlush = true;
     SendPacketGeneric(3, LastAck.data(), (int)LastAck.size(), LastAckTS);
+    HoldFlush = false;
     mprec::NResendAck++;
 }
 
diff --git a/src/net/LAN.h b/src/net/LAN.h
index 41a47a9..bc8ecd1 100644
--- a/src/net/LAN.h
+++ b/src/net/LAN.h
@@ -226,6 +226,7 @@ private:
     void SendNow(u32 type, const u8* packet, int len, u64 timestamp);
     void FlushDelayed();
     int ServiceDelayed(ENetEvent* event, int timeout);
+    bool HoldFlush = false;   // Pixelado 0012: SendNow queues without flushing (the ACK sent again goes with the next CMD)
 
     u32 FrameCount;
 
